  <AceProConnectionIllustrations slot="connection-illustrations" lang="en" />

  <h2>If Android doesn’t show the camera</h2>
  <p>Try a data cable and check that the camera is in U-Disk Mode. Some phones have an OTG setting you need to turn on. In the folder picker, look for the camera’s USB drive and its <code>DCIM</code> folder.</p>
  <p><a href="https://onlinemanual.insta360.com/acepro2/en-us/operation-tutorials/connect/connect-app">Insta360’s Ace Pro 2 USB connection instructions</a></p>

  <h2>What about Insta360 X4 or X5 360° videos?</h2>
  <p>Hikkonuki imports standard MP4 and MOV files from USB storage. It cannot read Insta360’s <code>.insv</code> 360° video files or stitch footage. Use the Insta360 app or Insta360 Studio to export those clips. Hikkonuki compatibility with the X4 and X5 is unverified.</p>
  <p><a href="https://onlinemanual.insta360.com/x5/en-us/operating-tutorials/storage/fileformat">Insta360’s X-series file formats</a></p>
</CameraGuide>
